chunks.concept:
The **total energy** of a system is its complete capacity to do work or cause change — the sum of **every** form of energy present.

Those forms include:

- **kinetic energy** — energy of motion;
- **potential energy** — stored energy of position or configuration (an object raised up, a spring squeezed);
- **thermal energy** — the energy of the random jiggling of particles (what we feel as temperature);
- **chemical energy** — energy stored in the bonds of fuel, food, or a battery;
- and others (electrical, light, sound, nuclear).

When we say energy is *conserved*, we mean this grand total never changes in a closed system — forms convert into one another, but the sum stays fixed. Energy is measured in **joules (J)** whatever form it is in.
